# frame-mini.hex — a voice Mini Frame.
#
# Hand-built octet by octet from RFC 5456 (provenance rule 1, Tests/FIXTURES.md).
#
# Header — 4 octets, RFC 5456 §8.1.2 Figure 6:
#
#   12 34        F = 0 (not a Full Frame) + 15-bit source call
#                number 0x1234 = 4660. The top bit of octet 0 is
#                clear, which is what distinguishes this from a Full
#                Frame; the first 16 bits are nonzero, which is what
#                distinguishes it from a Meta Frame              §8.1.2, §8.1.3.1
#   0b b8        16-bit time-stamp 0x0BB8 = 3000 ms — "the lower 16
#                bits of the transmitting peer's full 32-bit
#                time-stamp for the call"                            §8.1.2
#
# Payload — media only. A Mini Frame carries no destination call
# number, no sequence numbers, no frame type and no subclass; it is
# implicitly frame type 2 (Voice) and its codec is whatever the most
# recent full voice frame of the call named.                         §8.1.2
#
# 8 octets of G.711 µ-law stand in for a real 160-octet 20 ms frame
# (1 byte per sample at the default 8 kHz).                          §8.7, §8.6.32
#
1234 0bb8 ffffffff 7f7f7f7f
